Revision history for Markdown-Publish

1.005  2026-10-04

    - Rebase source-relative links from documents under doc/ to mirrored
      Markdown sidecars beneath lib/ and bin/ during site assembly.
    - Preserve existing publication-root links and leave authored Markdown,
      missing targets, unrelated paths, and code examples unchanged.

1.004  2026-09-29

    - Discover wrangler.jsonc or wrangler.json in the project root when
      Cloudflare publication configuration is not supplied explicitly.
    - Allow make publish_cloudflare to deploy with no Cloudflare settings in
      META_MERGE and document the minimal assets-only Wrangler configuration.

1.003  2026-09-26

    - Publish public repository metadata through the GitHub mirror.
    - Add contributor and security policies, dependency auditing and
      artifact-attestation verification guidance.
    - Declare the CPAN authority in distribution metadata.

1.002  2026-09-26

    - Initial release.
    - Publish the distribution as Markdown::Publish rather than
      ASPEER::Markdown::Publish.
    - Support MkDocs, VitePress, Docusaurus and Astro Starlight.
    - Keep site assembly, preview and publication independent of MakeMaker.
    - Add source selection, navigation, local-link rewriting and module aliases.
    - Support configured package commands, preview listeners and Pages base paths.
    - Prepare GitHub Pages content on a local gh-pages branch without pushing it.
    - Improve Starlight assembly, links, navigation and home-page promotion.
